ameed (Arabic: جميد), shilanch (Balochi: شیلانچ), chortan (Armenian: չորթան chort’an), aaruul or khuruud (Mongolian: ааруул or хурууд) is a range of dairy products popular in Iranian cuisine, Caucasian cuisine, and Central Asian cuisine. Kashk is made from strained yogurt, drained buttermilk (in particular, drained qatiq) or drained sour milk by shaping it and letting it dry. It can be made in a variety of forms: rolled into balls, sliced into strips, and formed into chunks."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-kashk"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kashk"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Tajik cuisine","cuisine/tajik-cuisine",[["Qurutob","dish/qurutob"]]]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/1/11/Jameed.JPG/500px-Jameed.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Syrinje","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jameed.JPG"}},"ingredient/pimento":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pimento","n":"Pimento","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The pimiento, or pimento, is a variety of red, heart-shaped chili pepper (Capsicum annuum) that measures 7–10 centimetres (3–4 inches) long and 2–3 centimetres (3⁄4–1+1⁄4 inches) wide."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pimento"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pimento"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Argentine cuisine","cuisine/argentine-cuisine",[["Salsa golf","dish/salsa-golf"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cumin","ingredient/cumin"],["Ketchup","ingredient/ketchup"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Oregano","ingredient/oregano"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/e/e1/Pimento_chilli.jpg/500px-Pimento_chilli.jpg","w":500,"h":328,"by":"Challiyan","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pimento_chilli.jpg"}},"dish/ulam-salad":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ulam-salad","n":"Ulam (salad)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Ulam is a traditional Malay salad produced from foraged leaves, vegetables or fruits which can be eaten raw or blanched e.g. Centella asiatica. It is typically eaten with sauces such as budu, cincalok or sambal.  It is popular in rural villages."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ulam-salad"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulam_(salad)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"],["Malay cuisine","cuisine/malay-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Leaf","ingredient/leaf"],["Vegetables","ingredient/vegetables"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/e/ef/Palembang_cuisine_Brengkes_Tempoyak_Lais_and_Pindang.jpg/500px-Palembang_cuisine_Brengkes_Tempoyak_Lais_and_Pindang.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Gunawan Kartapranata","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palembang_cuisine_Brengkes_Tempoyak_Lais_and_Pindang.jpg"}},"ingredient/sirloin":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sirloin","n":"Sirloin","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["In American butchery, the sirloin steak is a cut of beef from the sirloin, the subprimal posterior to the short loin where the  T-bone, porterhouse, and strip steaks are cut.  The sirloin is divided into several parts."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sirloin"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirloin"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Veal Milanese","dish/veal-milanese"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Rib chop","ingredient/rib-chop"]]}]},"dish/ziva-dish":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ziva-dish","n":"Ziva (dish)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Israeli cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Ziva is an Israeli dish made of puff pastry topped with  sesame seeds, and stuffed with cheese and olives. Ziva is served at home and in restaurants. Ziva is cooked in a style similar to the Yemenite Malawach but its ingredients more closely resemble börek, both of which are also common in Israel. Ziva is usually served alongside a hot sauce (skhug), eggs and Israeli salad."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ziva-dish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziva_(dish)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Israeli cuisine","cuisine/israeli-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Laminated dough","ingredient/laminated-dough"],["Nigella seeds","ingredient/nigella-seeds"],["Olive","ingredient/olive"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Sesame seeds","ingredient/sesame-seeds"]]},{"h":"More from Israeli cuisine","links":[["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Hummus","dish/hummus"],["Lahoh","dish/lahoh"],["Sabich","dish/sabich"],["Sufganiyah","dish/sufganiyah"],["Taboon bread","dish/taboon-bread"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/d/d7/Ziva-israelidish.jpg/500px-Ziva-israelidish.jpg","w":500,"h":427,"by":"Peteravivangel","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ziva-israelidish.jpg"}}}